<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<lpdf version="1"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="../../schema/lpdf.xsd">
  <assets>
    <font name="body"        core="Times-Roman" />
    <font name="body-italic" core="Times-Italic" />
    <font name="body-bold"   core="Times-Bold" />
    <font name="heading"     core="Helvetica-Bold" />
  </assets>
  <tokens>
    <colors>
      <color name="primary" value="#1763cf" />
      <color name="muted"   value="#737373" />
      <color name="rule"    value="#d4d4d4" />
      <color name="wash"    value="#eef3fb" />
    </colors>
  </tokens>
  <document size="a4" font="body">
    <meta title="lpdf Showcase — Markdown styles" subject="Rules that restyle a markdown, and its headings in a table of contents" />

    <!-- A rule is named after the Markdown it styles and takes the attributes of the element it becomes. The rules
         written here are laid over the default ones one attribute at a time, so what they do not set stays as it
         was. A document in an embedded font names the faces of the bold and the italic: em and strong.
         Expected, in order:
           Page 1  A cover section, a layout of its own, around the Markdown
           Page 2  The table of contents: Overview, Details and Notes at level 1 and 2 (bookmarks="2" keeps two
                   levels, so the third heading is not listed), each with its page
           Page 3  The Markdown in Times: headings in Helvetica Bold, h1 in blue with a rule's worth of space,
                   justified paragraphs with the italic and bold faces named, a list with square bullets,
                   a quote with a blue bar on a light wash, code on a blue-grey background, and a table with a wash
                   on its header cells and a light stripe
    -->
    <section>
      <layout margin="72pt">
        <column gap="l" justify="center" height="full">
          <text font="heading" font-size="xxl" color="primary">Markdown, restyled</text>
          <text color="muted">A cover section, a table of contents and the Markdown, in one document.</text>
        </column>
      </layout>
    </section>

    <section type="toc">
      <layout margin="72pt">
        <column gap="m">
          <text font="heading" font-size="xl" color="primary">Contents</text>
          <column gap="xs">
            <column data-source="$toc">
              <link href="#">
                <row justify="between">
                  <text data-value="label">Entry</text>
                  <text data-value="page" color="muted">0</text>
                </row>
              </link>
            </column>
          </column>
        </column>
      </layout>
    </section>

    <section>
      <layer>
        <rect x="0pt" y="0pt" width="595pt" height="10pt" fill="primary" />
        <text-at anchor="bottom-center" y="-24pt" font-size="xs" color="muted">Page {page} of {pages}</text-at>
      </layer>
      <markdown margin="72pt 72pt 60pt 72pt" gap="m" bookmarks="2">
        <markdown-styles>
          <h1 font="heading" color="primary" font-size="xxl" />
          <h2 font="heading" font-size="l" />
          <h3 font="heading" font-size="m" color="muted" />
          <p align="justify" line-height="1.5" />
          <em font="body-italic" />
          <strong font="body-bold" />
          <li bullet="square" gap="s" indent="20pt" />
          <quote color="primary" bar-color="primary" bar-width="4pt" background="wash" padding="4pt 4pt 4pt 8pt" />
          <code font="Courier" background="#eaf0f6" color="#1f3b57" />
          <a color="primary" underline="false" />
          <table stripe="wash" />
          <th font="heading" background="wash" font-size="s" padding="s" />
          <td font-size="s" padding="s" />
        </markdown-styles>
        <markdown-content><![CDATA[
          # Overview

          The *rules* of a markdown are **elements**, so the editor validates them, and a token file restyles them
          all. This paragraph is justified, and is long enough to wrap onto a few lines so that the spacing between
          its words shows, with the italic and the bold face of Times named in the rules of `em` and `strong`.

          ## Details

          - Square bullets from the `li` rule
          - A gap of `s` between items
            - A nested list, with the same indent
          - [A link](https://lpdf.io) without an underline

          > A quote on a wash, with a blue bar the height of the box and padding of its own.

          ### Not listed

          This heading is level 3, so with `bookmarks="2"` it is no bookmark and the contents do not list it.

          ## Notes

          ```
          rule  = element
          style = attributes
          ```

          | Rule   | Becomes  |
          |:-------|:---------|
          | `h1`   | a text   |
          | `code` | a box    |
          | `quote`| a table  |
        ]]></markdown-content>
      </markdown>
    </section>
  </document>
</lpdf>
